                <h2>适用场景与前置准备</h2>
<p>本 SOP 适用于 TikTok Shop 商家在新品上架后 0-30 天的冷启动阶段。冷启动期的核心目标是快速找到能跑量的素材方向，为后续放量奠定基础。</p>
<p><strong>前置准备清单：</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>确认新品核心卖点与差异化优势</li>
<li>梳理目标受众画像（年龄段、兴趣标签、消费能力）</li>
<li>备好产品实拍素材（白底图、开箱视频、使用场景视频）</li>
<li>开通 TikTok for Business 广告账户并完成基础投放配置</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>步骤一：明确素材方向与内容框架</h2>
<p>在动手拍摄前，先完成方向规划，避免盲目生产导致资源浪费。</p>
<h3>1.1 竞品素材拆解</h3>
<p>找到同类目在 TikTok 上表现较好的广告素材（可通过 TikTok Creative Center 或第三方工具查看）。重点记录：</p>
<ul>
<li>视频时长（建议 8-15 秒优先测试）</li>
<li>开篇前三秒的钩子形式（痛点共鸣、悬念、冲击力画面）</li>
<li>产品的核心展示角度</li>
<li>文案与字幕的调用方式</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.2 制定素材矩阵</h3>
<p>根据产品特性，规划 3-5 个不同方向的素材方向，每个方向至少储备 3 条素材：</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>方向类型</th>
<th>适用场景</th>
<th>示例</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>产品功能展示型</td>
<td>标品、功能明确的产品</td>
<td>开盖展示、效果对比</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>使用场景代入型</td>
<td>非标品、需要场景教育的</td>
<td>户外使用、厨房场景</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>痛点解决方案型</td>
<td>解决特定问题的产品</td>
<td>清洁效果、便携性演示</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>UGC 风格种草型</td>
<td>高颜值、有分享属性的产品</td>
<td>开箱反应、真人试用</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>限时促销型</td>
<td>有价格优势的新品</td>
<td>折扣信息、倒计时贴片</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>步骤二：素材生产与储备标准</h2>
<p>方向确定后，进入素材生产阶段。建议在冷启动前完成第一批量产。</p>
<h3>2.1 基础素材储备量</h3>
<ul>
<li>每个素材方向：3-5 条</li>
<li>总计：15-25 条原始素材</li>
<li>视频规格：建议 1:1（方形）和 9:16（竖版）各备一版，适配不同广告位</li>
</ul>
<h3>2.2 素材生产优先级</h3>
<p><strong>第一批（冷启动前 3 天完成）：</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>产品功能展示型 3 条</li>
<li>UGC 风格种草型 2 条</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>第二批（第 4-7 天补充）：</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>使用场景代入型 3 条</li>
<li>痛点解决方案型 2 条</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>第三批（根据数据反馈追加）：</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>效果好的方向追加 5 条</li>
<li>效果差的的方向调整角度或直接停用</li>
</ul>
<h3>2.3 素材质量要求</h3>
<ul>
<li>画面清晰，无过度压缩变形</li>
<li>开篇有吸引力，避免纯产品展示开头</li>
<li>字幕完整，关键信息（价格、卖点）突出</li>
<li>背景音乐适配TikTok流行趋势</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>步骤三：素材测试与快速筛选</h2>
<p>素材储备到位后，进入测试阶段，目的是用最小成本快速找到跑量素材。</p>
<h3>3.1 测试投放配置</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>账户结构：</strong> 建议每个素材方向单独建 Campaign，避免素材互相抢量</li>
<li><strong>预算分配：</strong> 初期每条素材日预算建议 20-50 美元，根据出单情况动态调整</li>
<li><strong>出价策略：</strong> 冷启动期建议使用最低成本出价（Lowest Cost），优先积累转化数据</li>
<li><strong>优化目标：</strong> 偏好选择“加购”或“结账”，而非直接选“购买”，以降低冷启动压力</li>
</ul>
<h3>3.2 数据监测节点</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>时间节点</th>
<th>监测重点</th>
<th>行动指引</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>投放后 6 小时</td>
<td>CTR 是否超过 1.5%</td>
<td>低于 1% 考虑暂停</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>投放后 24 小时</td>
<td>是否有转化</td>
<td>无转化但 CTR 正常可继续观察</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>投放后 48 小时</td>
<td>CPA 是否可接受</td>
<td>超出预期 2 倍以上暂停</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>投放后 72 小时</td>
<td>确定主力素材</td>
<td>CPA 低于目标 80% 的素材提量</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>3.3 素材筛选标准</h3>
<p>符合以下条件的素材保留并扩量：</p>
<ul>
<li>CTR ≥ 2%（种草类素材可适当放宽至 1.5%）</li>
<li>48 小时内至少 1 次转化</li>
<li>CPA 不超过目标 CPA 的 1.5 倍</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>步骤四：素材池管理与持续迭代</h2>
<p>冷启动不是一次性工作，需要建立素材池的持续更新机制。</p>
<h3>4.1 素材池分层管理</h3>
<p>建议将素材分为三层管理：</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>主力层：</strong> CPA 表现最优的前 20% 素材，持续投放并微调</li>
<li><strong>测试层：</strong> 新方向素材，持续小额测试</li>
<li><strong>淘汰层：</strong> 累计消耗 100 美元仍无转化的素材，移出主力池</li>
</ul>
<h3>4.2 素材更新节奏</h3>
<ul>
<li>每周至少补充 5-10 条新素材</li>
<li>每月进行一次素材方向复盘，淘汰效果下滑的方向</li>
<li>关注 TikTok 热门音乐和话题，借势更新背景音乐或字幕文案</li>
</ul>
<h3>4.3 素材复用技巧</h3>
<p>表现好的素材可以尝试：</p>
<ul>
<li>更换背景音乐或字幕文案，重新剪辑发布</li>
<li>将竖版素材裁剪为横版，投放 Discovery 广告位</li>
<li>将高 CTR 素材的钩子形式复用到其他产品</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>快速执行清单</h2>
<blockquote>
<p>完成新品冷启动素材池搭建，只需按顺序执行以下 8 件事：</p>
</blockquote>
<ol>
<li>✅ 梳理新品卖点与受众画像</li>
<li>✅ 拆解 5-10 条竞品爆款素材</li>
<li>✅ 制定 3-5 个素材方向矩阵</li>
<li>✅ 生产首批 10 条素材（功能+UGC 优先）</li>
<li>✅ 配置测试投放 Campaign，每条素材独立分组</li>
<li>✅ 48 小时后根据 CTR 筛选，保留高点击素材</li>
<li>✅ 一周后根据 CPA 确定主力素材并提量</li>
<li>✅ 每周固定补充新素材，保持 15-20 条在投库存</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>注意事项：</strong> 冷启动期不要同时测试超过 10 条素材，否则数据分散难以判断方向。优先聚焦 2-3 个最有把握的方向，集中验证后再扩大范围。</p>
            </div>
            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>Applicable Scenarios and Prerequisites</h2>
<p>This SOP applies to TikTok Shop sellers during the 0-30 day cold start phase after launching a new product. The core goal in cold start is to quickly identify high-performing creative directions as a foundation for scaling.</p>
<p><strong>Prerequisites Checklist:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Confirm core product selling points and differentiation advantages</li>
<li>Outline target audience profile (age, interests, spending capacity)</li>
<li>Prepare product photography assets (white background images, unboxing videos, usage scenario videos)</li>
<li>Set up TikTok for Business ad account with basic configurations complete</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Define Creative Direction and Content Framework</h2>
<p>Before shooting, complete direction planning to avoid wasted resources from blind production.</p>
<h3>1.1 Competitive Ad Analysis</h3>
<p>Find well-performing ad creatives from similar categories on TikTok (use TikTok Creative Center or third-party tools). Focus on recording:</p>
<ul>
<li>Video duration (8-15 seconds recommended for initial testing)</li>
<li>Hook format in the first 3 seconds (pain point resonance, suspense, impactful visuals)</li>
<li>Core product showcase angles</li>
<li>Caption and subtitle usage patterns</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.2 Build a Creative Matrix</h3>
<p>Based on product characteristics, plan 3-5 different creative directions, with at least 3 assets per direction:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Direction Type</th>
<th>Applicable Scenario</th>
<th>Example</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Product Feature Showcase</td>
<td>Standard products, items with clear functions</td>
<td>Cap opening demonstration, before/after comparison</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Usage Scenario Immersion</td>
<td>Non-standard products requiring context education</td>
<td>Outdoor usage, kitchen scenarios</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Pain Point Solution</td>
<td>Products solving specific problems</td>
<td>Cleaning effectiveness, portability demo</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>UGC Style Promotion</td>
<td>High-aesthetic, shareable products</td>
<td>Unboxing reactions, authentic try-ons</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Limited-Time Offer</td>
<td>New products with price advantages</td>
<td>Discount callouts, countdown overlays</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Asset Production and Inventory Standards</h2>
<p>With directions confirmed, move to production. Aim to complete initial batch before cold start launch.</p>
<h3>2.1 Baseline Inventory Requirements</h3>
<ul>
<li>Each creative direction: 3-5 assets</li>
<li>Total: 15-25 raw assets</li>
<li>Format: Prepare both 1:1 (square) and 9:16 (vertical) versions for different ad placements</li>
</ul>
<h3>2.2 Production Priority</h3>
<p><strong>Batch 1 (Complete 3 days before launch):</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Product feature showcase: 3 assets</li>
<li>UGC style promotion: 2 assets</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Batch 2 (Days 4-7 supplement):</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Usage scenario immersion: 3 assets</li>
<li>Pain point solution: 2 assets</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Batch 3 (Based on data feedback):</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>5 additional assets in high-performing directions</li>
<li>Pivot angles or discontinue underperforming directions</li>
</ul>
<h3>2.3 Quality Standards</h3>
<ul>
<li>Clear visuals, no excessive compression or distortion</li>
<li>Compelling opening—avoid starting with pure product shots</li>
<li>Complete subtitles with key info (price, selling points) highlighted</li>
<li>Background music aligned with TikTok trending sounds</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Asset Testing and Rapid Screening</h2>
<p>With inventory ready, enter the testing phase to identify high-performing creatives at minimum cost.</p>
<h3>3.1 Test Campaign Configuration</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Account Structure:</strong> Build separate Campaign per creative direction to prevent internal competition</li>
<li><strong>Budget Allocation:</strong> Initial daily budget of $20-50 per asset, adjust based on conversion data</li>
<li><strong>Bidding Strategy:</strong> Use Lowest Cost during cold start to accumulate conversion data faster</li>
<li><strong>Optimization Goal:</strong> Prefer "Add to Cart" or "Checkout" over "Purchase" to reduce cold start pressure</li>
</ul>
<h3>3.2 Monitoring Milestones</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Timeframe</th>
<th>Key Metrics</th>
<th>Action Guidelines</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>6 hours post-launch</td>
<td>CTR above 1.5%</td>
<td>Pause if below 1%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>24 hours post-launch</td>
<td>At least 1 conversion</td>
<td>Continue observing if CTR is normal</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>48 hours post-launch</td>
<td>CPA within acceptable range</td>
<td>Pause if exceeds target by 2x</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>72 hours post-launch</td>
<td>Identify主力素材</td>
<td>Scale assets with CPA below 80% of target</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>3.3 Screening Criteria</h3>
<p>Retain and scale assets meeting these conditions:</p>
<ul>
<li>CTR ≥ 2% (1.5% acceptable for awareness-style creatives)</li>
<li>At least 1 conversion within 48 hours</li>
<li>CPA does not exceed target CPA by more than 1.5x</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Material Library Management and Ongoing Iteration</h2>
<p>Cold start is not a one-time task—establish a continuous update mechanism for the material library.</p>
<h3>4.1 Tiered Library Management</h3>
<p>Manage assets in three tiers:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>主力层 (Main Tier):</strong> Top 20% by CPA performance—continue running with minor optimizations</li>
